Working's method is an innovative approach to estimating the correlation structure of longitudinal data within the Generalized Estimation Equations framework. Unlike traditional GEE methods, Working's method treats the correlation structure as a maximum likelihood estimate rather than a fixed parameter. This approach enables the estimation of correlations that are unique to each observation. In contrast to naive and iterative methods, Working's method is a faster but more accurate alternative. A software implementation of this method is available within the R package geepack, under the command gee(without iteration). 

